%% Runtime attestation, slice B: watching what was attested (runtime-attestation.md, "The plan"; outlined there, to be planned when
%% slice A is built). All designed, nothing built.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Op as Someone with access
    participant API as Kubernetes API
    participant Att as Attestation agent
    participant CA as Credentials agent
    participant Bk as Cassini broker

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Op,Att: DESIGNED: a pod changes after it was attested
    Att->>API: watching the pods it attested
    alt kubectl debug
        Op->>API: add an ephemeral container
        API-->>Att: the pod's status now shows it
    else a container restarted on another digest
        API-->>Att: the container's imageID is not what its Deployment pins
    end
    Att->>Att: the verdict is the attestation agent's: this instance has lapsed
    Att-)CA: published: this identity, this pod UID, and why
    CA->>CA: acting on it is the body guard's: stop renewing, so the certificate is dead within the hour
    opt the credentials agent, or an administrator's signed command, revokes sooner
        CA-)Bk: the revocation, through authority
        Bk->>Bk: end the session and refuse its next registration
    end
    end
